data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 11, the **sync-over-async opt-in for the EF Core Cosmos DB provider is removed entirely**. The Cosmos DB SDK is inherently async-only, and EF Core drops the internal `sync-over-async` bridge that the opt-in enabled.

All four of your methods will throw **`InvalidOperationException`** at runtime because `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, and `SaveChanges()` are synchronous calls against an async-only provider.

### Fix: convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `Add()` stays synchronous — it only tracks the entity in memory, no I/O.
- Callers must be updated to `await` these methods, which ripples `async` up the call stack.
- Remove the old `EnableSyncOverAsync()` / sync-over-async configuration — it's no longer recognized and may throw on startup.
